    "evidence": "Employee 4471's timesheet for the week commencing 19 October states breaks are unpaid and deducted from time on site, so worked hours are clock-out minus clock-in minus the unpaid break each day: Mon 08:00-16:30 = 8.50h - 0.50 = 8.00h; Tue 08:00-17:00 = 9.00h - 0.75 = 8.25h; Wed 07:30-16:00 = 8.50h - 0.50 = 8.00h; Thu 08:00-16:15 = 8.25h - 0.50 = 7.75h; Fri 08:00-17:00 = 9.00h - 0.50 = 8.50h. Total = 40.50 hours, not the 42 claimed: a 1.50 hour overstatement. No entries exist for Sat 24 or Sun 25 and no manual corrections were made. Alternatives checked: gross time on site before breaks is 43.25h, also not 42; to reach 42 the recorded 165 minutes of unpaid breaks would have to be only 75 minutes, which no entry supports; ignoring breaks per day and truncating to whole hours gives 39.00h; and no overtime is recorded, so there is no basis to add to the 40 contracted hours. Uncertainty acknowledged: if 'worked' were read as time on site rather than paid worked time the total would be 43.25h, still not 42; and this rests on the door-terminal clock times as recorded, so a manual correction or an additional shift would change the result. On the record as published the claim does not hold.",
